      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a decent start but i just ran it through our tool and the positivity score is actually pretty low—it's sitting at like 0.3. management is worried that because we mention \"salmonella\" and \"hospitalized\" or \"ill\" so much, it's going to look like we're spiraling.\n\ncan you try a second version? i still need it to be professional and not lie about what happened, but we really need to shift the tone so it doesn't look like a disaster on the sentiment metrics. try to rephrase things so they feel more focused on our proactive response and care rather than just the sickness itself. just keep it grounded, don't get weird with it.",
